enumeration under Native Image — exactly the concern the prior automation attempt flagged in its guidance. I have enough evidence now to finalize the decision.\n\n## Findings\n\nThe `tests/src/org.flywaydb/flyway-sqlserver/11.8.1` scaffold already contains an mssql-jdbc test dependency, a pinned `mssql/server` Docker image, and a `FixedResourceProvider` workaround for classpath resource enumeration. A prior automation run on this exact issue (preserved on branch `ai/kimeta/human-intervention/issue-9843-...`, visible via `git log`) reached the identical preflight conclusion — same dependency, same Docker image/slug — and that setup applied and built successfully (`setupDone: true`); the run later stalled for unrelated reasons (a \"reporter-requested metadata\" finalization step), not because of setup or a Native Image incompatibility. Separately, `org.flywaydb:flyway-core:13.5.0` (the base library) was already merged as supported under Native Image (`79917b7ed30`), so the SQL Server extension isn't inherently unsupportable. `flyway-sqlserver:13.5.0`'s POM declares no JDBC driver dependency (same as 11.8.1 — it's optional/BYO), and the mssql-jdbc/jackson-databind versions already pinned in the scaffold remain compatible (Flyway's own dependencyManagement pins mssql-jdbc 12.10.2.jre11 and legacy jackson-databind 2.22.2, but those aren't forced onto consumers). No mechanism (runtime codegen, agent self-attach, custom classloading, etc.) is present in the failure evidence — the issue log is truncated before any actual runtime error, so the unsupportable checklist fails at step 1.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"advisory_preparation\",\n  \"summary\": \"flyway-sqlserver needs a live SQL Server container plus an explicit JDBC driver dependency to exercise a real migration; the existing 11.8.1 scaffold already supplies both and a prior automation run validated the identical setup for 13.5.0.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"dependency\",\n      \"coordinate\": \"com.microsoft.sqlserver:mssql-jdbc:12.2.0.jre11\",\n      \"scope\": \"testImplementation\",\n      \"reason\": \"flyway-sqlserver does not bundle a JDBC driver (verified in its 13.5.0 POM); Flyway's own docs require a driver to be supplied separately, and the repository already trusts this exact driver version for this test.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"docker_image\",\n      \"image\": \"mcr.microsoft.com/mssql/server:2022-CU14-ubuntu-22.04\",\n      \"slug\": \"mssql_server\",\n      \"reason\": \"Meaningful migration coverage requires a real SQL Server instance; reuse the exact tag already pinned under tests/tck-build-logic/.../Dockerfile-mssql_server rather than introducing a new allow-list entry.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"Keep the existing FixedResourceProvider approach (hardcoded migration resource list) rather than relying on classpath resource enumeration, since GraalVM Native Image cannot enumerate classpath resources generically. Start the mssql/server container on 1433/tcp with ACCEPT_EULA=Y and a fixed SA password, poll until a JDBC connection succeeds (Awaitility, as in the current test) before invoking Flyway.migrate(), and tear the container process down in an @AfterAll. Run the migration through SQLServerDataSource against the two existing V1/V2 SQL migration resources and assert migrationsExecuted == 2. Note: the issue's reproducer command references coordinates=org.flywaydb:flyway-sqlserver:12.3.0 while the title/body target 13.5.0 — treat 13.5.0 as the authoritative target coordinate for local Gradle/Native Image verification.\",\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"Test requires Docker and exclusive use of host port 1433, consistent with the current scaffold.\",\n    \"Issue reproducer coordinate (12.3.0) does not match the stated target version (13.5.0); local verification should not be misled by the mismatch.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":4009,"type":"result","duration_ms":167004,"uuid":"cabb0856-5cd3-412e-bda6-a3bb486a3e2d","